Restored password sign-in on the login page. This add-on registers a route at `/login`, which replaces Volto's own, and the page offered external providers and the magic link only — so installing it took password sign-in away from every site with local accounts. On a site running the `[server]` layer that is not a rough edge but a dead end: an authorization server has to be able to authenticate its own users, and "sign in with somebody else" is not an answer it can give. A provider with no providers configured showed "No sign-in options are configured for this site" and no way in at all.

The password form now appears alongside the providers, behind a disclosure so the providers stay the headline, and on the empty-providers page as well. A refused attempt reports one message for a wrong login name and a wrong password alike, because telling them apart is an account-enumeration oracle. @ericof
